job-input-preflight notices
==========================

This package preflights caller files and inline JSON against the published
SameDayDesk useful-jobs catalog (PR51). It does not run the job engine and
does not grant purchase, network, or scheduler authority.

Pinned published inputs (read-only):
- client/public/for-agents/useful-jobs/catalog.json
- client/public/for-agents/useful-jobs/useful-jobs-1.0.0.tar.gz
- client/src/data/usefulJobsKit.json

The 8 MiB cap is aligned with useful-jobs 1.0.0 lib/validate-next-run.mjs
(MAX_LOCAL_INPUT_BYTES). Tests extract that archive and spawn
`node --eval` against the extracted module. This directory does not copy
F08 server/paid-useful-jobs/lib/input-guard.mjs (1 MiB Express-aligned cap)
or a competing useful-jobs kernel. Optional `--d01-root` imports SDS52
`inspectSample` from a read-only pin; it is not vendored here.

Fixture JSON under fixtures/vendor-budget-impact/ is a labeled SAMPLE copy
of kit samples/pricing/a (sibling SAMPLE.txt). That path is a refuse case.
Custom caller rows live under fixtures/caller/vendor-budget-impact/.

I01 (Neo PR54) hash-terms identity is `sha256:` + 64 hex. Integer digest
values are rejected. Bare 64-hex from validate-next-run currentInputs.sha256
is accepted as input.

Useful-jobs LICENSE/NOTICE inside the pinned archive remain authoritative
for that package. This module is MIT (see LICENSE).
